def row(c, v, verdict, prose): R[(c, v)] = (verdict, prose)

row(1, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'THESE ARE THE WORDS MOSES SPOKE TO ALL ISRAEL BEYOND THE JORDAN, IN THE WILDERNESS, IN THE ARABAH OPPOSITE SUPH, BETWEEN PARAN AND TOPHEL AND LABAN AND HAZEROTH AND DI-ZAHAB — THE PLACES READ AS THE SINS: the translation\'s thirty-three tokens for the Hebrew\'s twenty-two. {HP(1, 1, (("אלה", "הדברים", "אשר", "דבר", "משה"), "these are the words which Moses spoke — the phrase\'s five Bible seats, Exodus 19:6 and 35:1 the Torah\'s others (computed)"), (("אל", "כל", "ישראל", "בעבר", "הירדן"), "to all Israel beyond the Jordan — \'beyond the Jordan\' eleven Torah seats, nine this book\'s, twenty-six in the Bible (computed)"), (("במדבר", "בערבה", "מול", "סוף"), "in the wilderness, in the Arabah, OPPOSITE SUPH — Suph a place here (the store glosses it \'Red-Sea\'; the Sea of Reeds is two tokens at 1:40); the clause one seat (computed)"), (("בין", "פארן", "ובין", "תפל", "ולבן", "וחצרת"), "between Paran and Tophel and Laban and Hazeroth — Tophel the place at its one seat (the consonants stand at fourteen: plaster, folly); Hazeroth Numbers 33:17-18\'s station (computed)"), (("ודי", "זהב"), "and Di-zahab — TWO TOKENS in the DB, the store gluing the name (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 1, (("אוכח", "יתהון", "על", "דחבו", "במדברא"), "HE REBUKED THEM FOR THAT THEY HAD SINNED IN THE WILDERNESS — \'rebuked\' the book\'s one seat of the word (computed): the wilderness is not where he stood but what he charged"), (("ועל", "דארגיזו", "במישרא", "לקבל", "ים", "סוף"), "and for that they provoked in the plain opposite the Sea of Reeds — the Arabah made the plain of the provocation, Suph made the sea"), (("בפארן", "דאתפלו", "על", "מנא"), "IN PARAN WHERE THEY SCORNED THE MANNA — Tophel read as \'scorned\' (the Sifrei 1:13\'s \'words of folly they spoke against the manna\'); \'the manna\' three seats in the book (computed)"), (("ובחצרות", "דארגיזו", "על", "בשרא"), "and at Hazeroth where they provoked over the meat — Laban dropped, the quail\'s graves stood at Hazeroth (Numbers 11:35)"), (("ועל", "דעבדו", "עגל", "דדהב"), "AND FOR THAT THEY MADE THE CALF OF GOLD — Di-zahab read as the gold of the calf (the Sifrei 1:17); \'the calf\' 1:1 and 9:16 in the book (computed)"))} THE MOVE: the Sifrei 1:9-17 reads every place as a rebuke and the translation writes the reading into the verse — the Numbers walk found no such paraphrase in Onkelos Numbers; this is the book\'s first.')
row(1, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ELEVEN DAYS FROM HOREB BY THE WAY OF MOUNT SEIR TO KADESH-BARNEA. {HP(1, 2, (("אחד", "עשר", "יום", "מחרב"), "ELEVEN DAYS from Horeb — the parser [11]; the phrase one seat; \'from Horeb\' twelve seats (computed)"), (("דרך", "הר", "שעיר", "עד", "קדש", "ברנע"), "by the way of Mount Seir to KADESH-BARNEA — the name as two tokens only here and 1:19 (joined elsewhere); \'Mount Seir\' three Torah seats, all this speech\'s (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 2, (("מהלך", "חד", "עשר", "יומין"), "A JOURNEY OF eleven days — the translation supplies \'a journey\', one seat of the word in the book (computed)"), (("עד", "רקם", "גיאה"), "to REKAM GEYAH — the Aramaic name of Kadesh-barnea at its four seats (1:2, 1:19, 2:14, 9:23) (computed)"))} The Sifrei 2:1-2: eleven days\' distance become forty years — the retelling\'s measure.')
row(1, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'IN THE FORTIETH YEAR, IN THE ELEVENTH MONTH, ON THE FIRST OF THE MONTH, MOSES SPOKE ACCORDING TO ALL THAT THE LORD COMMANDED HIM — THE DATE AND THE RECEIPT. {HP(1, 3, (("ויהי", "בארבעים", "שנה", "בעשתי", "עשר", "חדש"), "and it was in the fortieth year, in the eleventh month — the parser [40, 11, 1] by the number reader (Numbers 33:38\'s \'in the year of the forty\' read [40, 5] by the ordinal reader: the two dates of the same year in two forms) (computed)"), (("באחד", "לחדש"), "on the first of the month — ten Torah seats (computed)"), (("ככל", "אשר", "צוה", "יהוה", "אתו", "אלהם"), "ACCORDING TO ALL THAT THE LORD COMMANDED HIM to them — the clause two seats: this and EXODUS 40:16, the tabernacle\'s receipt; the register\'s second receipt form, the seat filed NONE waiting for this reading (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 3, (("והוה", "בארבעין", "שנין", "בחד", "עשר", "ירחא"), "and it was in forty years, in the eleventh month — the translation keeps the number reader\'s form"), (("ככל", "די", "פקיד", "יי", "יתיה", "לותהון"), "according to all that the LORD commanded him to them — the receipt kept whole"))} The Sifrei 2:3 reads the eleventh month as the year\'s twelve; 2:8 reads \'all\' as the whole Torah\'s rules.')
row(1, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'AFTER HE HAD SMITTEN SIHON KING OF THE AMORITES WHO DWELT IN HESHBON, AND OG KING OF BASHAN WHO DWELT IN ASHTAROTH, IN EDREI. {HP(1, 4, (("אחרי", "הכתו", "את", "סיחן", "מלך", "האמרי"), "after he had smitten Sihon king of the Amorites — the clause one seat; Sihon and Og in one verse four (computed)"), (("בעשתרת", "באדרעי"), "in Ashtaroth, in Edrei — without the vav (Joshua 12:4 and 13:12 \'in Ashtaroth and in Edrei\') (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 4, (("בתר", "דמחא", "ית", "סיחון"), "after he had smitten Sihon"), (("עוג", "מלכא", "דמתנן"), "Og king of MATHNAN — Bashan\'s Aramaic name at sixteen seats (computed)"))} The Sifrei 3: the rebuke after the victories, so that none could say he rebuked from weakness.')
row(1, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'BEYOND THE JORDAN IN THE LAND OF MOAB MOSES TOOK UPON HIMSELF TO EXPLAIN THIS TORAH, SAYING. {HP(1, 5, (("הואיל", "משה", "באר"), "MOSES TOOK UPON HIMSELF TO EXPLAIN — the undertake-verb three seats (1 Samuel 12:22, Hosea 5:11), the store glossing \'yield\'; EXPLAIN the verb\'s three seats: this, 27:8 (\'very plainly\' on the stones) and Habakkuk 2:2 (\'make it plain on tablets\') — the consonants of \'well\' at thirty-eight seats, the store glossing \'dig\' (computed)"), (("את", "התורה", "הזאת", "לאמר"), "this Torah, saying — \'this Torah\' three Torah seats (1:5, 31:9, 31:11) (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 5, (("שרי", "משה", "פרש", "ית", "אולפן", "אוריתא"), "MOSES BEGAN TO EXPLAIN THE TEACHING OF THE TORAH — \'began\' five seats (1:5, 2:24, 2:31, 25:10, 33:20), \'the teaching\' one, \'the Torah\' twenty (computed)"))} The Sifrei 4: \'began\' a dispute — R. Judah: a beginning; the sages: an oath — the translation takes R. Judah\'s.')
row(1, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'THE LORD OUR GOD SPOKE TO US AT HOREB: YOU HAVE DWELT LONG ENOUGH AT THIS MOUNTAIN. {HP(1, 6, (("יהוה", "אלהינו", "דבר", "אלינו", "בחרב", "לאמר"), "the LORD our God spoke to us at Horeb, saying — the clause 1:6 and Jeremiah 26:16 (computed)"), (("רב", "לכם", "שבת", "בהר", "הזה"), "YOU HAVE DWELT LONG ENOUGH AT THIS MOUNTAIN — \'enough for you\' eight Bible seats: KORAH\'S TWICE (Numbers 16:3, 16:7), this, 2:3, 3:19, Jeroboam\'s, Ezekiel\'s; the singular \'enough for you\' once, 3:26 on Moses (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 6, (("סגי", "לכון", "דיתבתון", "בטורא", "הדין"), "ENOUGH FOR YOU that you have dwelt at this mountain — the Aramaic \'enough for you\' at 1:6, 2:3, 3:19 and the singular 3:26 (computed)"))} The Sifrei 5: \'enough\' read as reward (the tabernacle, the Torah, the elders), then as harm (idleness).')
row(1, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'TURN AND JOURNEY, GO TO THE HILL COUNTRY OF THE AMORITES AND ALL ITS NEIGHBORS — THE ARABAH, THE HILL, THE LOWLAND, THE NEGEB, THE COAST, THE LAND OF THE CANAANITE AND LEBANON, TO THE GREAT RIVER EUPHRATES. {HP(1, 7, (("פנו", "וסעו", "לכם", "ובאו"), "TURN AND JOURNEY and go — Numbers 14:25\'s words to the rejected generation, here the words at Horeb (the two seats of \'turn and journey for you\') (computed)"), (("בערבה", "בהר", "ובשפלה", "ובנגב", "ובחוף", "הים"), "in the Arabah, in the hill country, in the lowland, in the Negeb and on the coast of the sea — the five regions in one verse one seat (Joshua 10:40 and 12:8 the runs) (computed)"), (("עד", "הנהר", "הגדל", "נהר", "פרת"), "TO THE GREAT RIVER, THE RIVER EUPHRATES — GENESIS 15:18\'s words at their second seat, the covenant of the pieces (Joshua 1:4 plene) (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 7, (("אתפנו", "וטולו", "לכון", "ועולו"), "turn and travel for yourselves and go up"), (("ולבנן", "עד", "נהרא", "רבא", "נהרא", "פרת"), "and Lebanon to the great river, the river Euphrates — Lebanon kept as Lebanon here, THE SANCTUARY at 3:25 (computed)"))} The Sifrei 6: the regions as Mishnah Sheviit 9:2\'s; Lebanon a king and the Temple; the Euphrates\' waters.')
row(1, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'SEE, I HAVE SET THE LAND BEFORE YOU; GO IN AND POSSESS THE LAND THE LORD SWORE TO YOUR FATHERS, TO ABRAHAM, ISAAC AND JACOB, TO GIVE TO THEM AND THEIR SEED AFTER THEM. {HP(1, 8, (("ראה", "נתתי", "לפניכם", "את", "הארץ"), "SEE, I HAVE SET BEFORE YOU the land — one seat; \'see, I have set\' eight (2:24 Sihon, 30:15 life and death; Joseph\'s, Jericho\'s, Ai\'s) (computed)"), (("באו", "ורשו", "את", "הארץ"), "go in and possess the land — one seat (computed)"), (("לאברהם", "ליצחק", "וליעקב"), "to Abraham, to Isaac and to Jacob — the dative triad eleven Torah seats (computed)"), (("לתת", "להם", "ולזרעם", "אחריהם"), "to give to them and to their seed after them — one seat (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 8, (("חזי", "דיהבית", "קדמיכון", "ית", "ארעא"), "see that I have given before you the land"), (("עולו", "ואחסינו", "ית", "ארעא"), "go in and possess the land"))} The Sifrei 7-8: no weapons needed, only a surveyor; each patriarch worthy alone; \'after them\' David\'s and Jeroboam\'s conquests (Rabbi: the days of the Messiah).')
row(1, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'AND I SAID TO YOU AT THAT TIME: I CANNOT BEAR YOU ALONE. {HP(1, 9, (("ואמר", "אלכם", "בעת", "ההוא", "לאמר"), "and I said to you AT THAT TIME, saying — the refrain\'s first of ten seats in the three chapters (computed)"), (("לא", "אוכל", "לבדי", "שאת", "אתכם"), "I CANNOT BEAR YOU ALONE — one seat; Numbers 11:14\'s \'I am not able, I alone, to bear all this people\' and Jethro\'s \'you are not able to do it alone\' (Exodus 18:18) the kin (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 9, (("לית", "אנא", "יכיל", "בלחודי", "לסוברא", "יתכון"), "I am not able alone TO BEAR you — the bear-root at 1:9, 1:12, 1:31 twice, the Hebrew\'s carrying-verbs made one (computed)"))} The Sifrei 9:1: \'not from myself but from the mouth of the Holy One\' — the refrain of 5:1, 19:1, 25:6; 9:2: the judge liable in his person.')
row(1, 10, 'CONTEXT', f'THE LORD YOUR GOD HAS MULTIPLIED YOU, AND YOU ARE TODAY AS THE STARS OF HEAVEN FOR MULTITUDE. {HP(1, 10, (("והנכם", "היום", "ככוכבי", "השמים", "לרב"), "and behold you are today AS THE STARS OF HEAVEN FOR MULTITUDE — three seats, all this book\'s (1:10, 10:22, 28:62); \'as the stars of heaven\' six Torah seats (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 10, (("ככוכבי", "שמיא", "למסגי"), "as the stars of heaven for multitude"))} The Sifrei 10: \'today\' — you endure as the day; the seven classes of the righteous.')
row(1, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'THE LORD GOD OF YOUR FATHERS ADD TO YOU A THOUSAND TIMES AS MANY AS YOU ARE, AND BLESS YOU AS HE SPOKE TO YOU. {HP(1, 11, (("יסף", "עליכם", "ככם", "אלף", "פעמים"), "add to you A THOUSAND TIMES as you are — the parser [1000]; \'a thousand times\' one seat (computed)"), (("ויברך", "אתכם", "כאשר", "דבר", "לכם"), "and bless you as he spoke to you — one seat (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 11, (("יוסף", "עליכון", "כותכון", "אלף", "זמנין"), "add to you as you are a thousand times"))} The Sifrei 11: \'a thousand times\' is Moses\' blessing, \'as he spoke\' the LORD\'s unbounded one; the outside row 82:5 refuses to lengthen the priestly blessing by this verse.')
row(1, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'HOW CAN I BEAR ALONE YOUR TROUBLE AND YOUR BURDEN AND YOUR STRIFE? {HP(1, 12, (("איכה", "אשא", "לבדי"), "HOW can I bear alone — \'how\' (the Lamentations word) six Torah seats, GENESIS 3:9\'s \'where are you\' among them by the consonants (computed)"), (("טרחכם", "ומשאכם", "וריבכם"), "your TROUBLE and your burden and your strife — \'your trouble\' a hapax (the root\'s other seat Isaiah 1:14), \'your burden\' one seat, \'your strife\' one (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 12, (("אכדין", "אסובר", "בלחודי"), "how can I bear alone"), (("טרחכון", "ועסקיכון", "ודינכון"), "your trouble and YOUR BUSINESS AND YOUR JUDGMENTS — the burden read as business, the strife as lawsuits (computed)"))} The Sifrei 12: the troublesome litigant, the cynics who read Moses\' every step, the disputatious.')
row(1, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'GIVE YOURSELVES WISE AND UNDERSTANDING AND KNOWN MEN FOR YOUR TRIBES, AND I WILL SET THEM AS YOUR HEADS. {HP(1, 13, (("הבו", "לכם", "אנשים", "חכמים", "ונבנים", "וידעים"), "GIVE YOURSELVES men WISE AND UNDERSTANDING AND KNOWN — \'give yourselves\' four seats (Joshua 18:4, Judges 20:7, Ahithophel\'s); the three qualities against Jethro\'s four (Exodus 18:21) and 1:15\'s two (computed)"), (("ואשימם", "בראשיכם"), "AND I WILL SET THEM AS YOUR HEADS — one seat; the store reads \'and-put/set-them\' (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 13, (("גברין", "חכימין", "וסוכלתנון", "ומדען"), "men wise and understanding and known"), (("ואמננון", "רישין", "עליכון"), "and I will appoint them heads over you"))} The Sifrei 13: \'give\' is counsel; \'men\' excludes women; wise against understanding (the two money-changers); \'known to your tribes\'; \'I will set them\' — the revocalization \'their guilt on your heads\'.')
row(1, 14, 'CONTEXT', f'AND YOU ANSWERED ME AND SAID: THE THING YOU HAVE SPOKEN IS GOOD TO DO. {HP(1, 14, (("ותענו", "אתי", "ותאמרו"), "and you answered me and said — one seat; the store glosses the answer-verb \'and-eye\' (the homograph) (computed)"), (("טוב", "הדבר", "אשר", "דברת", "לעשות"), "the thing you have spoken is good to do — one seat (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 14, (("תקין", "פתגמא", "די", "מללתא", "למעבד"), "the thing you spoke is right to do"))} The Sifrei 14: you should have asked to learn from Moses himself; you rejoiced at judges to bribe.')
row(1, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'AND I TOOK THE HEADS OF YOUR TRIBES, WISE AND KNOWN MEN, AND MADE THEM HEADS OVER YOU: CAPTAINS OF THOUSANDS, HUNDREDS, FIFTIES, TENS, AND OFFICERS FOR YOUR TRIBES. {HP(1, 15, (("ואקח", "את", "ראשי", "שבטיכם"), "and I took the heads of your tribes — 1:15 and 5:23 (computed)"), (("אנשים", "חכמים", "וידעים"), "men WISE AND KNOWN — two qualities where 1:13 asked three (\'understanding\' not found — the Sifrei 15:2) (computed)"), (("שרי", "אלפים", "ושרי", "מאות", "ושרי", "חמשים", "ושרי"), "captains of thousands AND captains of hundreds AND captains of fifties AND captains — with the vavs, one seat; Exodus 18:21 and 25 without them; the parser [100, 50, 10], the thousands a plural noun (computed)"), (("ושטרים", "לשבטיכם"), "AND OFFICERS FOR YOUR TRIBES — one seat; the officers-word thirteen Torah seats (Exodus 5\'s foremen, Numbers 11:16\'s seventy) (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 15, (("רבני", "אלפין", "ורבני", "מאותא"), "masters of thousands and masters of hundreds"), (("וסרכין", "לשבטיכון"), "and officers for your tribes"))} The Sifrei 15: Jethro\'s seven qualities, three found; the heads honored; the commanders by rounding down; the officers the Levites with the lash.')
row(1, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'AND I CHARGED YOUR JUDGES AT THAT TIME: HEAR BETWEEN YOUR BROTHERS AND JUDGE RIGHTEOUSLY BETWEEN A MAN AND HIS BROTHER AND HIS STRANGER. {HP(1, 16, (("ואצוה", "את", "שפטיכם", "בעת", "ההוא", "לאמר"), "and I charged your judges at that time, saying — one seat (computed)"), (("שמע", "בין", "אחיכם", "ושפטתם", "צדק"), "HEAR BETWEEN YOUR BROTHERS AND JUDGE RIGHTEOUSLY — each clause one seat (computed)"), (("בין", "איש", "ובין", "אחיו", "ובין", "גרו"), "between a man and his brother and HIS STRANGER — \'his stranger\' two Bible seats, this and Exodus 6:4\'s \'their sojournings\' by the consonants; the lemma\'s eighty-three (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 16, (("שמעו", "בין", "אחיכון", "ותדונון", "קושטא"), "hear between your brothers and judge IN TRUTH — \'in truth\' one seat in the book (computed)"), (("ובין", "גיוריה"), "and his stranger — the Aramaic keeps the stranger, one seat (computed)"))} The Sifrei 16: deliberate in judgment (Avot 1:1); the judges indentured to the public; R. Ishmael and the gentile litigant; the righteous claimant brings proof; \'a man\' excludes a minor; \'his stranger\' four readings.')
row(1, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'YOU SHALL NOT RECOGNIZE FACES IN JUDGMENT; SMALL AND GREAT ALIKE YOU SHALL HEAR; YOU SHALL NOT BE AFRAID OF A MAN, FOR THE JUDGMENT IS GOD\'S; THE HARD MATTER BRING TO ME. {HP(1, 17, (("לא", "תכירו", "פנים", "במשפט"), "YOU SHALL NOT RECOGNIZE FACES IN JUDGMENT — 1:17 and 16:19 (the judges\' law) (computed)"), (("כקטן", "כגדל", "תשמעון"), "SMALL AND GREAT ALIKE you shall hear — the pair\'s one Torah seat (computed)"), (("לא", "תגורו", "מפני", "איש"), "YOU SHALL NOT BE AFRAID of a man — the fear-verb by the lemma, the store glossing the sojourn-root\'s homograph (computed)"), (("כי", "המשפט", "לאלהים", "הוא"), "FOR THE JUDGMENT IS GOD\'S — one seat (computed)"), (("והדבר", "אשר", "יקשה", "מכם", "תקרבון", "אלי"), "and the matter too hard for you bring to me — \'the hard matter\' (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 17, (("לא", "תשתמודעון", "אפין", "בדינא"), "you shall not show favor in judgment — one seat (computed)"), (("מלי", "זערא", "כרבא", "תשמעון"), "WORDS small as great you shall hear — the Aramaic supplies \'words\'"), (("ארי", "דינא", "דיי", "הוא"), "for the judgment is THE LORD\'S"))} The Sifrei 17: the appointer of judges; the poor man\'s and the rich man\'s dignity refused; silence before hearing, none after; compromise a dispute; the hard matter — Zelophehad\'s daughters, Samuel the seer.')
row(1, 18, 'CONTEXT', f'AND I CHARGED YOU AT THAT TIME ALL THE THINGS YOU SHOULD DO. {HP(1, 18, (("ואצוה", "אתכם", "בעת", "ההוא"), "and I charged you at that time — the refrain (computed)"), (("את", "כל", "הדברים", "אשר", "תעשון"), "all the things which you shall do (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 18, (("ית", "כל", "פתגמיא", "די", "תעבדון"), "all the things that you shall do"))} The Sifrei 18:1: the ten distinctions between money cases and capital cases (Sanhedrin 4:1).')
row(1, 19, 'MATERIAL', f'AND WE JOURNEYED FROM HOREB THROUGH ALL THAT GREAT AND TERRIBLE WILDERNESS, AS THE LORD COMMANDED US, AND CAME TO KADESH-BARNEA. {HP(1, 19, (("ונסע", "מחרב", "ונלך"), "and we journeyed from Horeb and went — the first person plural, the speech retelling (computed)"), (("את", "כל", "המדבר", "הגדול", "והנורא", "ההוא"), "all THAT GREAT AND TERRIBLE WILDERNESS — plene one seat (8:15 defective) (computed)"), (("ונבא", "עד", "קדש", "ברנע"), "and we came to KADESH-BARNEA — the second two-token seat (computed)"))} → {AP(1, 19, (("מדברא", "רבא", "ודחילא", "ההוא"), "that great and fearful wilderness"), (("ואתינא", "עד", "רקם", "גיאה"), "and we came to Rekam Geyah"))} The Sifrei 18:2: serpents like beams, scorpions like bows — a fortiori for the ordinary.')
